Package: studysynth
Title: Synthesize Fake 'REDCap' Study Data Without Touching Real Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Nate", "Vack", email = "nate@gimlet.us", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads a 'REDCap' project's structure (metadata-only project
    XML or the data dictionary, events, and instrument mapping CSVs) and a
    'YAML' spec describing how items relate ('lavaan' syntax), how people
    change over time ('lme4'-style formulas), screening, dropout, partial
    sessions, and experience sampling. Synthesizes as many imaginary
    participants as you like, in 'REDCap' import format, so analysis code
    can be written and tested before real data exist. It never reads real
    subject data.
